# Podcast production processor tick -- every 5 minutes
# The controller IS the processor; the scheduler IS its heartbeat. Each tick
# runs scripts/podcast_scheduler_runner.sh, which sources the podcast env and
# runs podcast_controller.py --once over queued TaskFlows. ONE entry PER BOX
# (not per client): the per-client once-daily law (guard-cron-inventory.py)
# governs openclaw client crons only; this box-level tick is recognized by
# name 'podcast-scheduler' and excluded from the per-client census.
# Env vars: PODCAST_ENV_FILE, PODCAST_CONTROLLER_PATH, PODCAST_SCHEDULER_LOG,
#           PODCAST_SCHEDULER_DRY_RUN
# User field: the OpenClaw runtime user (node by default; PODCAST_NODE_USER
# elsewhere). The controller writes node-owned state; config writes never run
# as root. On macOS the launchd agent (config/launchd/) is the idiom instead.
*/5 * * * * node /usr/local/bin/podcast-scheduler-runner.sh
